      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1868 Spanish colonists built the Church of San Ysidro, named after the annual May fiesta, still a historic landmark.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Corrales%2C_New_Mexico",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The village incorporated in 1971 but was fully annexed to Sandoval County in 2005, unifying its governance.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21,
